				{
					"name": "Get All Users",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{token}}"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"users"
							]
						},
						"description": "Retrieves the complete list of users from the backend.\n\n## HTTP Request\n- **Method:** `GET`\n- **URL:** `{{baseUrl}}/users`\n\n## Authentication\nThis endpoint requires Bearer token authentication.\n\nSet the `Authorization` header:\n```http\nAuthorization: Bearer {{token}}\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `{{token}}` is a valid access token for the authenticated user/session.\n\n## Path & Query Parameters\n- **Path parameters:** None\n- **Query parameters:** None (the endpoint currently returns all users without filtering or pagination).\n\n## Successful Response (200 OK)\nOn success, the endpoint returns:\n- **Status:** `200 OK`\n- **Body:** JSON array of user objects.\n\n### User object fields\nEach item in the array has (at least) the following fields:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"dd8fdc42-fa5f-4010-8e38-57e521030423\",\n    \"firstName\": \"Marco\",\n    \"lastName\": \"Manfrin\",\n    \"email\": \"marco.manfrin04@gmail.com\",\n    \"role\": \"OWNER\",\n    \"type\": \"TECHNICIAN\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n- `id` (string): Unique identifier of the user.\n- `firstName` (string): User's first name.\n- `lastName` (string): User's last name.\n- `email` (string): User's email address.\n- `role` (string): High-level role of the user in the system (for example, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `USER`).\n- `type` (string): Functional type/category of the user (for example, `TECHNICIAN`, `SELLER`, `ADMINISTRATION`).\n\nThe response body will contain an array with zero or more user objects following this structure."
					},
					"response": []
				},
